  { title: 'The spice will humble you', desc: 'Sichuan mala isn\'t just heat — the peppercorns make your tongue tingle and go numb, a sensation unlike anything in Thai, Indian, or Mexican food. Non-spicy dishes exist, but half the menu bites back. Pack antacids and embrace the burn.' },
  { title: 'English is scarce outside hotels', desc: 'Restaurant menus rarely have English. Taxi drivers won\'t understand you. Street vendors definitely won\'t. Download a translation app with camera translation, and always carry your hotel address in Chinese. Google Translate\'s offline Chinese pack works without VPN.' },
  { title: 'Pandas nap through midday', desc: 'The famous pandas are most active 8:00–10:00 AM. By 11:30, most are asleep — not "cute sleepy," but "barely visible furry lump." If you arrive at 1 PM expecting action, you\'ll be disappointed. Set an early alarm.' },
  { title: 'Summer is punishing', desc: 'July–August brings 30°C+ heat, punishing humidity, and domestic summer holidays. Temple courtyards become ovens. Spring (Mar–May) and autumn (Sep–Nov) are 15–25°C and dramatically more pleasant.' },
