const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is the best time to visit Chengdu?', a: 'Spring (March–May) and autumn (September–November) are ideal: 15–25°C, low rainfall, and golden ginkgo trees in fall. Summer is hot and humid but is baby panda season. Winter is gray and damp but uncrowded. See our month-by-month table above for details.' },
  { q: 'How many days do I need in Chengdu?', a: 'Minimum 2 full days for the essentials (pandas, ancient streets, hotpot, and opera). Three to four days lets you add a day trip to the Leshan Giant Buddha or Mount Qingcheng. If you\'re a food-focused traveler, give yourself at least 3 days — you\'ll want to eat six meals a day.' },
  { q: 'Is Chengdu safe for tourists?', a: 'Yes, Chengdu is very safe. Violent crime against tourists is extremely rare. Standard precautions apply: watch for pickpockets in very crowded markets, use official taxis or Didi at night, and keep your passport secure. Solo female travelers report feeling safe.' },
  { q: 'What is Chengdu famous for?', a: 'Three things above all: giant pandas (Chengdu is the global panda capital), Sichuan cuisine (hotpot, mapo tofu, dan dan noodles — a UNESCO City of Gastronomy since 2010), and tea house culture (Chengdu invented tea culture as we know it, over 1,000 years ago).' },
  { q: 'Do I need a visa for Chengdu?', a: 'Most visitors need a Chinese tourist visa (L visa). Chengdu now offers a 144-hour (6-day) transit visa waiver for travelers from 54 countries transiting to a third country. Always check the latest policy with your local Chinese embassy — rules change.' },
  { q: 'Should I visit Chengdu or Chongqing?', a: 'Pick Chengdu for food, pandas, tea culture, and a laid-back pace. Pick Chongqing for jaw-dropping cityscapes, the spiciest hotpot on earth, and Yangtze River cruises. They\'re connected by a 1.5-hour high-speed train — many travelers do both. See our detailed comparison table above.' },
  { q: 'Which panda base should I visit?', a: 'Chengdu Research Base for the most pandas (~200), the baby nursery, and easy Metro access. Dujiangyan Panda Base for a quieter, open-air experience and the hands-on volunteer keeper program. If you only have one panda day: Chengdu for the spectacle, Dujiangyan for the experience. Full comparison above.' },
  { q: 'How much does a trip to Chengdu cost?', a: 'Backpacker: ¥200–300/day (hostel, street food, Metro, one attraction). Mid-range: ¥500–800/day (boutique hotel, restaurants, Didi, all attractions). Luxury: ¥800+/day (five-star, fine dining, private driver). Chengdu is one of China\'s most affordable major cities.' },
  { q: 'Can I use credit cards or Apple Pay in Chengdu?', a: 'Not widely. WeChat Pay and Alipay dominate, and both now accept foreign credit cards (link in-app before you travel). Cash is accepted everywhere. Carry some RMB for small street-food stalls and local markets. ATMs that take foreign cards are at major banks and airports.' },
  { q: 'Is English widely spoken in Chengdu?', a: 'Limited. Hotel front desks and younger locals may speak basic English, but restaurant staff, taxi drivers, and market vendors generally do not. Download a translation app with camera translation. Have key addresses saved in Chinese characters on your phone. See our first-timer mistakes above.' },
  { q: 'What should I pack for Chengdu?', a: 'Comfortable walking shoes, umbrella, passport, VPN (installed before arriving), translation app with offline Chinese pack, tissues, power bank, and an adventurous appetite. See our full packing checklist above for the complete rundown.' },
  { q: 'Is Chengdu worth visiting if I only have a short time in China?', a: 'Yes — especially if you love food. Even one full day (pandas, ancient streets, one hotpot dinner, one tea house) gives you a taste of what makes Chengdu special. Two days is better. Three days and you\'ll start planning your return before you leave.' },
  { q: 'How do I get from Chengdu airport to the city center?', a: 'Shuangliu Airport (CTU): Metro Line 10 connects directly to the city in about 20–30 minutes (¥5–7). Taxi/Didi costs ¥50–70 and takes 25–40 minutes. Tianfu Airport (TFU): The new airport is farther — Metro Line 18 takes 45–50 minutes (¥10–12), taxi ¥150–200 and 50–70 minutes. Both airports have clear English signage.' },
  { q: 'Is the tap water safe to drink in Chengdu?', a: 'No. Tap water in Chengdu is not potable — locals boil it first or use bottled water dispensers. Hotels provide bottled water or electric kettles. Convenience stores sell 1.5L bottles for ¥2–4. Restaurants serve boiled water or tea by default. Ice is generally made from purified water at reputable establishments, but skip it at street stalls if you\'re cautious.' },
  { q: 'What is the air quality like in Chengdu?', a: 'Chengdu sits in a basin surrounded by mountains, so air quality can be poor — especially in winter (Dec–Feb). AQI frequently ranges 100–180 (unhealthy for sensitive groups) during winter months. Spring and summer are better (AQI 50–100). If you have asthma or respiratory issues, bring medication and check real-time AQI on apps like AirVisual. Many locals wear masks on high-AQI days — it\'s normal and not cause for alarm.' },
  { q: 'Is Chengdu good for families traveling with kids?', a: 'Yes — Chengdu is one of China\'s most family-friendly cities. The Panda Base is a guaranteed hit with children. People\'s Park has playgrounds and paddle boats. The Sichuan Science and Technology Museum (free, near Tianfu Square) has hands-on exhibits. Most hotpot restaurants offer non-spicy broth options. The Metro is stroller-accessible with elevators at every station. Fewer stairs and hills than Beijing or Chongqing.' },
  { q: 'Where can I go shopping in Chengdu?', a: 'Chunxi Road (春熙路) is the main pedestrian shopping street — massive malls, international brands, and the IFS building with the famous climbing panda sculpture. Taikoo Li (太古里) next door is upscale open-air luxury boutiques in modern architecture. Jinli Street and Kuanzhai Alley for souvenirs (Sichuan embroidery, panda merch, tea). Songxianqiao Antique Market on weekends for curios and Cultural Revolution memorabilia.' },
  { q: 'How do I access the internet in Chengdu? (VPN, SIM cards, WiFi)', a: 'Install and test a VPN before leaving home — you cannot download VPN apps once in China. ExpressVPN and Astrill are most reliable. For mobile data: buy a China Unicom or China Mobile SIM at the airport (¥100–200 for 20–50GB). Alternatively, get an eSIM (Airalo, Holafly) before arriving — no VPN needed for eSIM data. Hotel WiFi requires VPN for Google/Instagram/WhatsApp. Download offline Google Maps and Google Translate Chinese pack before you arrive as backup.' },
];

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  'datePublished': '2026-07-29',
  'dateModified': '2026-08-05',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'WebPage',
      name: 'Best of Chengdu 2026 — Complete Local Guide to Food, Attractions, Pandas & Travel Tips',
      description: 'The most comprehensive Chengdu travel guide for 2026. Sichuan restaurant recommendations with specific dishes and addresses, panda base comparison table, month-by-month weather calendar, honest first-timer advice, photo spots, packing list, and real traveler reviews.',
      url: 'https://best-of-chengdu.com/',
      speakable: {
        '@type': 'SpeakableSpecification',
        cssSelector: ['h1', '.hero-subtitle'],
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://best-of-chengdu.com/' },
      ],
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'Best of Chengdu',
      url: 'https://best-of-chengdu.com/',
      description: 'A locally researched, regularly updated guide to the very best of Chengdu, Sichuan — curated food recommendations with specific restaurants, attraction guides, and honest travel advice.',
      sameAs: [],
    },
    {
      '@type': 'FAQPage',
      mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: faq.q,
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: faq.a,
        },
      })),
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  schemaJson={JSON.stringify(schema)}
  title="2026 Complete Chengdu Guide — Best Food, Attractions, Pandas & Local Tips"
  description="The most comprehensive Chengdu guide for 2026. Specific restaurant recommendations, panda base comparison, month-by-month weather, honest first-timer advice, photo spots, packing list, and real traveler reviews. Plan your trip to China's food capital."
>
  <Header />

  <main>
    <!-- ===== HERO ===== -->
    <section class="relative">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-surface"></div>
      <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto relative">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0 min-h-[520px] md:min-h-[640px] items-stretch">
          <div class="flex flex-col justify-center px-6 md:px-12 py-20 md:py-0">
            <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-accent mb-4">Updated August 2026 · Our team explored Chengdu in person</p>
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tighter leading-[1.05] text-[#1a1a1a] max-w-[14ch]">
              Best of Chengdu <span class="text-accent">2026</span>
            </h1>
            <p class="hero-subtitle mt-5 text-base md:text-lg text-gray-500 leading-relaxed max-w-[48ch]">
              Everything you need to plan an unforgettable trip to China's food capital — where to eat (with specific restaurant names), which panda base to choose, what to really expect, and how to avoid the mistakes everyone makes.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
              <a href="#food" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-accent text-white px-7 py-3.5 rounded-full text-sm font-medium hover:bg-accent-dark transition-colors duration-150">
                What to eat
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
              </a>
              <a href="#attractions" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-border text-gray-700 px-7 py-3.5 rounded-full text-sm font-medium hover:border-accent/30 hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-150">
                See attractions
              </a>
              <a href="#mistakes" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-border text-gray-700 px-7 py-3.5 rounded-full text-sm font-medium hover:border-accent/30 hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-150">
                Avoid mistakes
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="relative overflow-hidden min-h-[300px] md:min-h-0">
            <img
              src="/images/hero.webp"
              alt="Traditional red lanterns along a Chengdu street with Sichuan-style architecture"
              class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-[50%_30%]"
              loading="eager"
              width="1200"
              height="800"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== STICKY SECONDARY NAV ===== -->
    <nav id="subnav" class="sticky top-16 z-40 bg-white/90 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-border overflow-x-auto">
      <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6 flex items-center gap-1 py-2 text-xs font-medium whitespace-nowrap">
        <a href="#food" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-gray-500 hover:text-accent hover:bg-accent/5 transition-colors">Food</a>
        <a href="#attractions" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-gray-500 hover:text-accent hover:bg-accent/5 transition-colors">Attractions</a>
        <a href="#pandas" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-gray-500 hover:text-accent hover:bg-accent/5 transition-colors">Pandas</a>
        <a href="#plan" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-gray-500 hover:text-accent hover:bg-accent/5 transition-colors">Plan</a>
        <a href="#itineraries" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-gray-500 hover:text-accent hover:bg-accent/5 transition-colors">Itineraries</a>
        <a href="#mistakes" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-gray-500 hover:text-accent hover:bg-accent/5 transition-colors">Mistakes</a>
        <a href="#photos" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-gray-500 hover:text-accent hover:bg-accent/5 transition-colors">Photos</a>
        <a href="#faq" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-gray-500 hover:text-accent hover:bg-accent/5 transition-colors">FAQ</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- ===== TABLE OF CONTENTS ===== -->
    <section class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6 pt-12 md:pt-16 pb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-gray-400 mb-4">On This Page</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a href="#food" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-accent/5 text-accent hover:bg-accent/10 transition-colors">🍜 What to Eat</a>
        <a href="#attractions" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-gray-50 text-gray-600 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">🏯 Attractions</a>
        <a href="#pandas" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-gray-50 text-gray-600 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">🐼 Panda Comparison</a>
        <a href="#plan" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-gray-50 text-gray-600 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">📅 Plan Your Trip</a>
        <a href="#itineraries" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-gray-50 text-gray-600 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">🗺️ Itineraries</a>
        <a href="#vs-chongqing" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-gray-50 text-gray-600 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">⚖️ Chengdu vs Chongqing</a>
        <a href="#mistakes" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-gray-50 text-gray-600 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">⚠️ Mistakes to Avoid</a>
        <a href="#photos" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-gray-50 text-gray-600 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">📸 Photo Spots</a>
        <a href="#expect" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-gray-50 text-gray-600 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">💡 What to Expect</a>
        <a href="#faq" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-gray-50 text-gray-600 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">❓ FAQ</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== QUICK FACTS ===== -->
    <section class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6 pt-8 pb-16 md:pb-20">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-2 reveal">Chengdu at a Glance</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-500 mb-8 reveal">Everything you need to know before you go — in 30 seconds.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        {quickFacts.map((fact) => (
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-white hover:border-accent/20 transition-colors duration-200">
            <span class="block text-xs font-medium tracking-wide uppercase text-gray-400 mb-1">{fact.label}</span>
            <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] leading-snug">{fact.value}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== WHY VISIT CHENGDU ===== -->
    <section class="bg-surface py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="max-w-[740px]">
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6 reveal">Why Visit Chengdu?</h2>
          <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed reveal">
            <p>Let's be honest — most people come to Chengdu for two things: <strong class="text-[#1a1a1a]">giant pandas</strong> and <strong class="text-[#1a1a1a]">Sichuan food</strong>. Both live up to the hype. But neither is the real reason you'll remember this city.</p>
            <p>Chengdu <span class="text-[#1a1a1a] font-medium">(成都, Chéngdū)</span> has existed for over 2,200 years without changing its name — one of the oldest continuously named cities on earth. Twenty-one million people live here, and they've figured out something the rest of China hasn't: <em>life is supposed to be enjoyed, not just endured</em>. Walk through People's Park on a Tuesday afternoon. You'll see old men playing mahjong under ginkgo trees, couples dancing to a portable speaker, families sipping jasmine tea for three hours without checking a phone. Nobody is rushing. Nobody looks stressed. This is the Chengdu way — and it's contagious.</p>
            <p>UNESCO named Chengdu a <strong class="text-[#1a1a1a]">City of Gastronomy</strong> in 2010 — one of only about 50 cities worldwide. Walk any street at 7 PM and the air smells of chili oil and Sichuan peppercorns. Mapo tofu was born here in 1862 at a shop still serving it today. Kung pao chicken — the real version, not the gloopy takeout — was invented in a Chengdu courtyard kitchen. Hotpot restaurants have lines at midnight. This isn't a city where you eat to live. This is a city that <em>lives to eat</em>.</p>
            <p>The pandas are everything you hope they'll be — 200 of them at the Chengdu Research Base, 30 minutes from downtown. But here's what surprised us: the city's tea houses might be even more memorable. Heming Tea House in People's Park has been serving jasmine tea in covered cups for over a century. Old men bring their pet birds in bamboo cages. The tea costs ¥15 and you can sit for four hours. Nobody will rush you. This tradition is over 1,000 years old — Chengdu essentially invented tea culture as we know it.</p>
            <p>Then there's the Sichuan Opera — face-changing performers who whip colored silk masks across their faces faster than your eye can track. The clatter of mahjong tiles in every park. A nightlife scene that runs past 3 AM. And two of China's finest day trips: the 71-meter Leshan Giant Buddha carved into a red cliff in the 8th century, and Mount Qingcheng — a mist-shrouded Taoist mountain where stone staircases disappear into clouds. Both under two hours from downtown.</p>
            <p class="text-[#1a1a1a] font-medium">Chengdu isn't a city you tick off a checklist. It's a city you sink into — and then spend the rest of your trip telling people they need to come here too.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== FOOD ===== -->
    <section id="food" class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-2 reveal">What to Eat in Chengdu — And Where</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg max-w-[52ch] mb-10 reveal">Eight dishes that define Sichuan cuisine. Each one comes with a specific restaurant recommendation — because knowing <em>what</em> to order is only half the battle.</p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10 reveal">
        {mustTryDishes.map((dish) => (
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-border bg-white hover:border-accent/20 hover:shadow-sm transition-all duration-200">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-2 mb-1.5">
              <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-[#1a1a1a]">{dish.name}</h3>
              <span class="text-[11px] text-accent/70 font-medium">{dish.where}</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">{dish.desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <!-- Food image -->
      <div class="mt-10 mb-8 reveal max-w-[860px]">
        <img
          src="/images/food-hotpot.webp"
          alt="Sichuan hotpot bubbling with chili oil, sliced meats, and vegetables — the quintessential Chengdu dining experience"
          class="w-full rounded-2xl object-cover max-h-[420px]"
          loading="lazy"
          width="1200"
          height="600"
        />
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6 reveal">Explore by category</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 reveal">
        {foodCategories.map((cat) => (
          <a href={cat.href} class="group flex flex-col p-5 rounded-xl border border-border hover:border-accent/30 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-200">
            <h4 class="font-display font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] group-hover:text-accent transition-colors">{cat.label}</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">{cat.desc}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== ATTRACTIONS ===== -->
    <section id="attractions" class="bg-surface py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-2 reveal">Top Attractions in Chengdu</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg max-w-[52ch] mb-8 reveal">From giant pandas to ancient temples — with ticket prices, transit, and honest timing advice for each one.</p>

        <!-- Attractions image -->
        <div class="mt-10 mb-8 reveal max-w-[860px]">
          <img
            src="/images/jinli-lanterns.webp"
            alt="Red lanterns glowing above Jinli Ancient Street at dusk, traditional Sichuan architecture with cobblestone lanes"
            class="w-full rounded-2xl object-cover max-h-[420px]"
            loading="lazy"
            width="1200"
            height="600"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3 max-w-[860px] reveal">
          {topAttractions.map((attraction, i) => (
            <a href={attraction.href} class="block p-5 rounded-xl bg-white border border-border hover:border-accent/20 hover:shadow-sm transition-all duration-200 group">
              <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
                <span class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5">{i + 1}</span>
                <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap mb-1">
                    <span class="font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] text-sm group-hover:text-accent transition-colors">{attraction.name}</span>
                    <span class="text-[10px] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent font-medium shrink-0">{attraction.tag}</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-1.5">{attraction.desc}</p>
                  <span class="text-[11px] text-gray-400">{attraction.price}</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== HIDDEN GEMS ===== -->
    <section id="hidden-gems" class="bg-surface py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-2 reveal">Hidden Gems — Beyond the Tourist Trail</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg max-w-[52ch] mb-10 reveal">Six places most visitors miss — ancient temples, surreal architecture, and creative quarters that locals actually go to on weekends.</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 reveal">
          {hiddenGems.map((gem) => (
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-white hover:border-accent/20 hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-200 flex flex-col overflow-hidden">
              <img
                src={gem.img}
                alt={gem.alt}
                class="w-full h-48 object-cover"
                loading="lazy"
                width="600"
                height="400"
              />
              <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-1">
                <span class="text-[10px] font-medium text-accent bg-accent/5 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full self-start mb-2">{gem.tag}</span>
                <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-[#1a1a1a] mb-1.5">{gem.name}</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed flex-1 mb-3">{gem.desc}</p>
                <span class="text-[11px] text-gray-400 flex items-center gap-1">📍 {gem.tip}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== PANDA BASE COMPARISON ===== -->
    <section id="pandas" class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-2 reveal">Which Panda Base Should You Visit?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg max-w-[52ch] mb-10 reveal">Two bases, two very different experiences. Here's the detailed comparison to help you choose.</p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto reveal">
        <table class="w-full max-w-[860px] text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-border">
              <th class="text-left py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-gray-400 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide w-[28%]"></th>
              <th class="text-left py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] w-[36%]">Chengdu Research Base</th>
              <th class="text-left py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] w-[36%]">Dujiangyan Panda Base</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {pandaBaseComparison.map((row) => (
              <tr class="border-b border-border/50">
                <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-gray-500">{row.feature}</td>
                <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-[#1a1a1a] leading-relaxed">{row.chengdu}</td>
                <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-[#1a1a1a] leading-relaxed">{row.dujiangyan}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- Panda image -->
      <div class="mt-10 mb-8 reveal max-w-[860px]">
        <img
          src="/images/panda-eating.webp"
          alt="Giant panda sitting and eating bamboo in soft morning light at the Chengdu Research Base"
          class="w-full rounded-2xl object-cover max-h-[420px]"
          loading="lazy"
          width="1200"
          height="600"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mt-10 reveal max-w-[860px]">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-accent/5 border border-accent/10">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] mb-2">Pick Chengdu if…</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-500">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span> You want to see as many pandas as possible (~200)</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span> Seeing baby pandas in the nursery is a priority</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span> You're short on time (30 min Metro from downtown)</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span> You're visiting with young children</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-accent/5 border border-accent/10">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] mb-2">Pick Dujiangyan if…</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-500">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span> You want the hands-on volunteer keeper program</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span> You prefer a quiet, uncrowded hillside experience</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span> You're combining with Mount Qingcheng or the Irrigation System</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0">→</span> Open-air enclosures for clearer photos (no glass)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4 reveal max-w-[860px]"><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Can you do both?</span> Yes — and many visitors do. Morning at Chengdu Research Base, afternoon train to Dujiangyan, volunteer day the next morning. If you only have one panda day: Chengdu for the spectacle, Dujiangyan for the experience.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== EXPERIENCES ===== -->
